   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law, in relation\nto requiring harness racetrack locations awarded a gaming facility license\nmaintain live racing activity",
    "basePrintNo": "S8358",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8358-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1355, RWB L",
    "lawSection": "Racing, Pari-Mutuel Wagering and Breeding Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8358\n\nSPONSOR: ADDABBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law, in\nrelation to requiring harness racetrack locations awarded a gaming\nfacility license maintain live racing activity\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis legislation will require harness racetrack locations awarded a full\ngaming facility license to maintain live racing activity.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 creates a new paragraph (c) of subdivision 1 of section 1355\nof the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law to require harness\nracetrack locations awarded a gaming facility license maintain live\nracing activity.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nWith the expansion of pending full-license casinos in New York State, it\nis essential that those sites that presently have racetrack locations\ncontinue to offer live racing activity. The Racing Industry in New York\nState provides more than 19,000 direct jobs and $3 billion annual impact\nto the State. This bill would clarify and remove any vagueness or poten-\ntial confusion in terms of racing activity.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE. HISTORY:\n\n2023/24- S5342/A4907: Senate Racing, Gaming & Waging Committee / Assem-\nbly rules\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
